  "format": "pinmame-harness-scenario",
  "notes": "Boot a Pirates of the Caribbean ROM from an empty NVRAM and enter the S.A.M. switch test with the named Back and Select service keys (Back, then Select five times: service-menu splash, icon menu, diagnostics menu, switch menu, switch test). The scenario names no game, so one byte-identical file serves every potc_* driver it is run against (potc_600af, the known-working table's ROM, and potc_110af). Every public switch starts at 0. Hold 1 (Left Lane, an ordinary switch) and then each of the seven printed optos, 3, 4, 11, 21, 22, 60 and 61, for 3 s with a snapshot while held and another 2 s after release, then 3 and 1 again. The switch test prints the name of a switch when the ROM reads it as active and NONE when it does not, and its 16x4 grid marks every matrix switch the ROM reads as active; the Avengers LE control scenario avs-switch-test-loki-control.json shows that both report the ROM's logical reading rather than the raw public level. The held addresses lie in the playfield matrix, outside every cabinet input the named keys drive.",
